  "gate": "Toothed horizontal opening: unchanged gate.png closed master; runtime LCP uses same-size gate.webp. Deterministic full-canvas left/right/frame extraction remains on PNG masters. See gate-masks.json and extract-gates.py. No generated art or hidden surface synthesis.",
  "buttons": "Static only: new preview assets empty; generated masters not registered.",
  "webp_conversion": "Every runtime art file is WebP; the PNGs stay as masters and are never shipped. Lossy q95 (alpha_quality 100) is used only when it is at least 1.5x smaller than lossless AND holds PSNR >= 36 dB over non-transparent pixels with an untouched alpha plane; otherwise the encoder falls back to lossless, which decodes to pixel-identical RGB/alpha. AVIF was measured on the same assets and rejected: it drifted the alpha plane by up to 12 levels (0.5-6.7 % of pixels) at no size advantage."
